hat chances  are there's a little scrub bar at the  bottom that's gonna let you really move  through the movies a lot quicker  I'll move through photos of these slides  and things like that even though that  touch bar looks really nice with its  OLED display and its matte glass finish  it does like I mentioned before replace  the function keys that were there  previously so if you're like me who does  use those function keys quite a bit to  switch between apps and programs it's  kind of a bummer because it's not as  easy to switch through programs as it  was before that's basically all the  touch bar really does it's just there to  give you different graphics and  different logos to kind of get you more  invited into the program I guess and to  speed up the process sometimes if you  get used to it it probably does help you  speed up the process a lot more but  personally I haven't used it that much  to be able to really tell you guys if  it's worth it if it's going to speed up  your workflow enough to justify the  difference but in my personal opinion I  don't think that an extra five hundred  dollars for a touch bar that just gives  you different graphics instead of  learning keyboard shortcuts is worth the  money and that's my review of the math  book touch bar if you enjoyed the video  make sure you smash that subscribe  button maybe drop a comment let me know  what you'd like to see next and  hopefully I'll see you next Monday  you
 

